WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.992
Composition feeds one output into another function

00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:06.695
Let g add two, and let f square its input

00:00:06.695 --> 00:00:14.100
In f of g of x, g acts first, so its entire output becomes the input to the squaring rule.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.908
For input three, the inner function produces five, then the outer function squares five to produce twenty five

00:00:21.908 --> 00:00:29.500
Replacing the whole input gives f of g of x equals the square of x plus two, including its cross term.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.461
Reverse the order and the same starting input now produces eleven

00:00:35.461 --> 00:00:38.426
Squaring three gives nine before adding two

00:00:38.426 --> 00:00:46.900
Because the operations do different things, composition generally depends on order and cannot be replaced by multiplying the two functions.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.903
A composition must satisfy every stage of its domain

00:00:51.903 --> 00:00:59.719
If the outer function is instead a real square root, the inner output x plus two must be nonnegative

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:03.833
This restricts the original input to negative two or larger.
